(71274, 2276, 1024, '<td valign="top">I only gave 2 10''s this week, and this was one of them.</td>', 'I only gave 2 10''s this week, and this was one of them.', '2002-06-10 15:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(71275, 2276, 641, '<td valign="top">Yes! I love this! This is what I had in mind, but didn''t have the resource to pull it off.  I love the colors and feeling in this shot.</td>', 'Yes! I love this! This is what I had in mind, but didn''t have the resource to pull it off.  I love the colors and feeling in this shot.', '2002-06-10 15:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(71276, 2276, 1528, '<td valign="top">nice tones<br/>nice composition</td>', 'nice tonesnice composition', '2002-06-10 15:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(71277, 2276, 772, '<td valign="top">Testing a new critique method with your photo:<br/><br/>Composition and Framing: I see absolutely no problems with this photo on either of these issues.  The subject is very nicely placed on the ''third'' line and also nicely centered vertically in the frame.  The vertical centring allows the ''road'' to have the visibility it needs in this challenge.  I also really appreciate the way the shadow provides a nice diagonal in the frame.  This diagonal helps draw attention to the subject.  <br/><br/>Image quality:  The image quality on this photo is also very nice.  Everything is crisp and clear, as it should be in this type of photograph.  The tones of blue that you have in your sky are very nice.  Possibly a bit darker blue would have been nice but that is just my preference.  <br/><br/>Challenge:  This photo has done an excellent job of meeting the challenge.  I expected to see something like this, but this is a good thing!  Your impression of what I ''expected'' to see is indeed beyond my expectation.  <br/><br/>Note:  One of my photography mentors has always told me that a photograph should generally read like a book - from left to right and from top to bottom.  With this in *my* mind, I would possibly attempted to do this shot with the hiker placed on the ''left'' third line and walking towards me instead of away from me.  This is just a thought of my own personal opinion. <br/><br/>Now that I have tried my critique method on your photo, I think i like it.  I obviously can''t comment this way on everything, but maybe i will try it more in the future... btw - i scored this shot a 10.. i really like it!  good job!</td>', 'Testing a new critique method with your photo:Composition and Framing: I see absolutely no problems with this photo on either of these issues.  The subject is very nicely placed on the ''third'' line and also nicely centered vertically in the frame.  The vertical centring allows the ''road'' to have the visibility it needs in this challenge.  I also really appreciate the way the shadow provides a nice diagonal in the frame.  This diagonal helps draw attention to the subject.  Image quality:  The image quality on this photo is also very nice.  Everything is crisp and clear, as it should be in this type of photograph.  The tones of blue that you have in your sky are very nice.  Possibly a bit darker blue would have been nice but that is just my preference.  Challenge:  This photo has done an excellent job of meeting the challenge.  I expected to see something like this, but this is a good thing!  Your impression of what I ''expected'' to see is indeed beyond my expectation.  Note:  One of my photography mentors has always told me that a photograph should generally read like a book - from left to right and from top to bottom.  With this in *my* mind, I would possibly attempted to do this shot with the hiker placed on the ''left'' third line and walking towards me instead of away from me.  This is just a thought of my own personal opinion. Now that I have tried my critique method on your photo, I think i like it.  I obviously can''t comment this way on everything, but maybe i will try it more in the future... btw - i scored this shot a 10.. i really like it!  good job!', '2002-06-10 15:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(71278, 2276, 327, '<td valign="top">Niccccccce composition, color, clear, clean, crisp shot! Good work.</td>', 'Niccccccce composition, color, clear, clean, crisp shot! Good work.', '2002-06-10 16:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(71279, 2276, 2091, '<td valign="top">Nice Capture, Looks like something from a magazine :)</td>', 'Nice Capture, Looks like something from a magazine :)', '2002-06-10 18:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(71280, 2276, 1078, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  I''m hoping he didn''t have as far to haul his saddle as the photo makes it look.  My only "I wish" with the photo is that the plant on the left edge weren''t there.  Maybe it''s because his shadow leads directly to it, but I look at it more than I think it deserves.  It also makes the photo feel a touch less barren.  Very minor, though, and I''m being nitpicky.</td>', 'Very nice.  I''m hoping he didn''t have as far to haul his saddle as the photo makes it look.  My only "I wish" with the photo is that the plant on the left edge weren''t there.  Maybe it''s because his shadow leads directly to it, but I look at it more than I think it deserves.  It also makes the photo feel a touch less barren.  Very minor, though, and I''m being nitpicky.', '2002-06-10 19:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(71281, 2276, 1005, '<td valign="top">Wow, another great shot!  Great color!  (fantastic color)  Among the top 10 easily.  Photo 10 Creativity 9 Road 10 total 10<br/>(kinda works for next week, too! but weakly)</td>', 'Wow, another great shot!  Great color!  (fantastic color)  Among the top 10 easily.  Photo 10 Creativity 9 Road 10 total 10(kinda works for next week, too! but weakly)', '2002-06-10 20:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
