(71347, 2277, 1455, '<td valign="top">jmsetzler wins the "guess the meaning of the title" challenge, Thank you John. Lot''s of others tie in the "find the mis-spelled word" challenge. And a few very special people  made spectacular achievments in the "look at picture, put ''mind'' to work" category. I will not explain the "joke", that the title refers to. Sorry. As for how this photo pertains to the challenge, I have this to say to the nice folks that gave me ones or twos due to there short ''comings''.<br/><br/>"The next time that you are traveling "On the road" and you look up and see a "green light", please consider the danger you may impose on others if and when you decide to convince yourselves that that light has nothing to do with being "On the road."<br/><br/>I wish that you all know that the outcome of this challenge will not in any way cause me to hold a grudge toward any other user on this site, as many of us my have noticed a naked man doing recently.<br/><br/>My photo was a bit abstract. It was found on the road and easy to shoot from my ladder.<br/><br/>Oh yeah. It''s a green light!</td>', 'jmsetzler wins the "guess the meaning of the title" challenge, Thank you John. Lot''s of others tie in the "find the mis-spelled word" challenge. And a few very special people  made spectacular achievments in the "look at picture, put ''mind'' to work" category. I will not explain the "joke", that the title refers to. Sorry. As for how this photo pertains to the challenge, I have this to say to the nice folks that gave me ones or twos due to there short ''comings''."The next time that you are traveling "On the road" and you look up and see a "green light", please consider the danger you may impose on others if and when you decide to convince yourselves that that light has nothing to do with being "On the road."I wish that you all know that the outcome of this challenge will not in any way cause me to hold a grudge toward any other user on this site, as many of us my have noticed a naked man doing recently.My photo was a bit abstract. It was found on the road and easy to shoot from my ladder.Oh yeah. It''s a green light!', '2002-06-17 03:05:00.000000', NULL, 0),
